{"profiles":[{"commonNames":[{"language":"en","name":"Bourke's parrot","source":"Wikipedia"}],"gbif":{"canonicalName":"Neopsephotus","confidence":94,"rank":"genus","scientificName":"Neopsephotus Mathews, 1912","status":"ACCEPTED","usageKey":2479794},"ottId":108569,"rank":"genus","scientificName":"Neopsephotus","synonyms":[],"wikipedia":{"extract":"Bourke's parrot (Neopsephotus bourkii, formerly known as Neophema bourkii), also known as the blue-vented parrot, sundown parrot, pink-bellied parrot, Bourke's parakeet, Bourke or \"Bourkie\", is a small parrot found in Australia and the only species in its genus, Neopsephotus. It is approximately 19 cm long and weighs around 45 grams.","revisionId":1356522538,"title":"Bourke's parrot","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bourke%27s_parrot","wikidataId":"Q848617"}},{"commonNames":[{"language":"en","name":"Gee’s Golden Langur","source":"The IUCN Red List of Threatened Species"},{"language":"en","name":"Golden Langur","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Golden Leaf Monkey","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Gee s Golden Langur","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Gee's Golden Langur","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Gee's Golden Lutung","source":"Catalogue of Life"}],"gbif":{"canonicalName":"Trachypithecus geei","confidence":99,"rank":"species","scientificName":"Trachypithecus geei Khajuria, 1956","status":"ACCEPTED","usageKey":2436536},"ottId":118937,"rank":"species","scientificName":"Trachypithecus geei","synonyms":["Presbytis geei","Trachypithecus geei bhutanensis","Trachypithecus geei geei"],"wikipedia":{"extract":"Gee's golden langur (Trachypithecus geei), also known as simply the golden langur, is an Old World monkey found in a small region of Western Assam, India and the neighboring foothills of the Black Mountains of Bhutan. Long considered sacred by many Himalayan people, the golden langur was first brought to the attention of the Western world by the naturalist Edward Pritchard Gee in the 1950s.","revisionId":1361533729,"title":"Gee's golden langur","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gee%27s_golden_langur","wikidataId":"Q284104"}},{"commonNames":[{"language":"en","name":"Golden-brown Mouse Lemur","source":"The IUCN Red List of Threatened Species"},{"language":"en","name":"Ravelobe Mouse Lemur","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Lac Ravelobe Mouse Lemur","source":"Catalogue of Life"}],"gbif":{"canonicalName":"Microcebus ravelobensis","confidence":99,"rank":"species","scientificName":"Microcebus ravelobensis Zimmerman, Ehresmann, Zeitemann, Radespiel, Randrianambinina & Rakotoarison, 1997","status":"ACCEPTED","usageKey":4266976},"ottId":148505,"rank":"species","scientificName":"Microcebus ravelobensis","synonyms":[],"wikipedia":{"extract":"The golden-brown mouse lemur (Microcebus ravelobensis), also known as the (Lac) Ravelobe mouse lemur, is part of the Cheirogaleidae family, and the smallest species of lemur. It is arboreal, nocturnal and usually social.","revisionId":1356978324,"title":"Golden-brown mouse lemur","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden-brown_mouse_lemur","wikidataId":"Q673062"}},{"commonNames":[],"gbif":{"canonicalName":"Melignomon","confidence":94,"rank":"genus","scientificName":"Melignomon Reichenow, 1898","status":"ACCEPTED","usageKey":2478654},"ottId":173465,"rank":"genus","scientificName":"Melignomon","synonyms":[],"wikipedia":{"extract":"Melignomon is a genus of birds in the family Indicatoridae.","revisionId":1345587921,"title":"Melignomon","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Melignomon","wikidataId":"Q2409776"}},{"commonNames":[{"language":"en","name":"Barn Owls","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Barn-Owls","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Barn Owl","source":"Martha's Vineyard species checklist"}],"gbif":{"canonicalName":"Tytonidae","confidence":94,"rank":"family","scientificName":"Tytonidae","status":"A